<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vicente Guerrero</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1782">1782</a>–<a href="/years/1831">1831</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vicente <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrero">Guerrero</a> was a leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-war-of-independence">Mexican War of Independence</a> who kept up <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> resistance in the south after 1815. In 1821 he joined the royalist officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agustin-de-iturbide">Agustín de Iturbide</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plan-of-iguala">Plan of Iguala</a>, which brought independence. As president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> in 1829 he abolished <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>, but he was overthrown that year and executed by the conservative government in 1831.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vicente-guerrero.jpg" alt="Vicente Guerrero" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anacleto Escutia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vicente_Guerrero.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
